    "['vrf-target [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'vrf definition v1', 'parent_command': ['route-target import [parameter1]'], 'root': 'route-target import [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper `set routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nvrf definition v1\\n rd 10.10.3.4:1\\n route-target both 100:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, VRF configuration is done under `vrf definition` context\\n2. I included the `rd` (route distinguisher) command as well since it\\'s required for proper VRF operation and was specified in the original Juniper configuration (`set routing-instances v1 route-distinguisher 10.10.3.4:1`)\\n3. The `route-target both` command is the Cisco equivalent of Juniper\\'s `vrf-target`, with \"both\" indicating import/export of routes with this target', 'trans_template': 'vrf definition v1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'rd 10.10.3.4:1', 'parent_command': ['route-target import [parameter1]'], 'root': 'route-target import [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper `set routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nvrf definition v1\\n rd 10.10.3.4:1\\n route-target both 100:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, VRF configuration is done under `vrf definition` context\\n2. I included the `rd` (route distinguisher) command as well since it\\'s required for proper VRF operation and was specified in the original Juniper configuration (`set routing-instances v1 route-distinguisher 10.10.3.4:1`)\\n3. The `route-target both` command is the Cisco equivalent of Juniper\\'s `vrf-target`, with \"both\" indicating import/export of routes with this target', 'trans_template': 'rd 10.10.3.4:1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-target both 100:1', 'parent_command': ['route-target import [parameter1]'], 'root': 'route-target import [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper `set routing-instances v1 vrf-target target:100:1` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nvrf definition v1\\n rd 10.10.3.4:1\\n route-target both 100:1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, VRF configuration is done under `vrf definition` context\\n2. I included the `rd` (route distinguisher) command as well since it\\'s required for proper VRF operation and was specified in the original Juniper configuration (`set routing-instances v1 route-distinguisher 10.10.3.4:1`)\\n3. The `route-target both` command is the Cisco equivalent of Juniper\\'s `vrf-target`, with \"both\" indicating import/export of routes with this target', 'trans_template': 'route-target both 100:1'}]]": 1,
